WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.872
We were headed west, toward the Indian Ocean, and the Nautilus was traveling quickly.

2
00:00:05.873 --> 00:00:11.134
Where would Captain Nemo's whim carry us next? Only time would tell.

3
00:00:11.135 --> 00:00:16.713
Every day we were charmed by some new marvel that we saw through the windows of the submarine.

4
00:00:16.714 --> 00:00:23.293
Ned kept trying to vary our diet by introducing some of the foods we had gathered on our island excursion.

5
00:00:23.294 --> 00:00:29.285
Aside from that, we no longer thought about life on land until something very strange happened.

6
00:00:29.286 --> 00:00:35.452
On January 18, I went up to the platform to greet the day as was my habit.

7
00:00:35.453 --> 00:00:41.364
I waited for the lieutenant to call out his usual phrase, but this time the words were different.

8
00:00:41.365 --> 00:00:49.118
Almost immediately Captain Nemo appeared and scanned the horizon with his telescope. For some minutes he didn't move.

9
00:00:49.119 --> 00:00:55.943
Then he lowered his telescope and exchanged some words with his lieutenant, who appeared agitated.

10
00:00:55.944 --> 00:00:58.856
The captain, however, remained cool.

11
00:00:58.857 --> 00:01:04.840
What had they seen with their telescopes? I looked carefully at the horizon but could see nothing.

12
00:01:04.841 --> 00:01:08.594
The Nautilus was hundreds of miles from the nearest shore.

13
00:01:08.595 --> 00:01:13.578
Pacing the platform, Captain Nemo gave the order for the submarine to speed up.

14
00:01:13.579 --> 00:01:17.595
Just then the lieutenant drew the captain's attention to something. Captain

15
00:01:17.596 --> 00:01:22.657
Nemo stopped pacing and studied the horizon again with his telescope. I

16
00:01:22.658 --> 00:01:29.308
had to find out what they were looking at. I went to the gallery and retrieved a telescope that I often used. Back

17
00:01:29.309 --> 00:01:36.316
on the platform, I raised it to my eye, but as soon as I did that, the telescope was snatched away! I

18
00:01:36.317 --> 00:01:40.737
turned around to face Captain Nemo, but I almost didn't recognize him. His

19
00:01:40.738 --> 00:01:46.649
eyes flashed and his teeth were clenched. His whole body betrayed his anger. He

20
00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:50.633
did not move while my telescope rolled at his feet. Had

21
00:01:50.634 --> 00:01:55.554
I unwittingly discovered some secret that provoked this fit of anger? I

22
00:01:55.555 --> 00:02:00.888
quickly realized that I was not the object of his hatred because he wasn't looking at me. His

23
00:02:00.889 --> 00:02:04.881
gaze was fixed on some distant point of the horizon. "Professor

24
00:02:04.882 --> 00:02:12.190
Aronnax," he said in a particularly commanding tone, "I now require you to honor your agreement with me." "What

25
00:02:12.191 --> 00:02:14.793
do you mean?" I asked. "You

26
00:02:14.794 --> 00:02:19.960
and your companions must be confined until I decide to release you." "You're

27
00:02:19.961 --> 00:02:26.690
the captain," I said while looking steadily at him. "But may I ask you one question?" "You

28
00:02:26.691 --> 00:02:28.261
may not." It

29
00:02:28.262 --> 00:02:31.507
would have been useless to try to resist his order. I

30
00:02:31.508 --> 00:02:37.269
went down to the cabin occupied by Ned and Conseil and told them what the captain had said. You

31
00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:41.848
can imagine Ned's reaction, but there was no time for argument. Four

32
00:02:41.849 --> 00:02:48.261
of the crew arrived and conducted us to that cell where we had spent our first night onboard the Nautilus .

33
00:02:48.262 --> 00:02:52.499
Ned tried to protest, but the door was shut in his face.

34
00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:57.325
"Master, will you tell us what this all means?" asked Conseil.

35
00:02:57.326 --> 00:03:03.817
I had no idea what was going on and could only think of the strange fear on Captain Nemo's face.

36
00:03:03.818 --> 00:03:08.246
"Hello! What's this?" said Ned, interrupting my thoughts.

37
00:03:08.247 --> 00:03:14.079
"Breakfast! But it's only the regular ship's fare, none of my special treats from the island."

38
00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:19.730
"I suggest we eat it," said Conseil, "because we don't know when we'll see our next meal."

39
00:03:19.731 --> 00:03:27.389
We took our seats at the table and ate in silence. Just then the ceiling light went out, leaving us in total darkness.

40
00:03:27.390 --> 00:03:32.381
"That's all right," said Ned. "I'm feeling sleepy anyway."

41
00:03:32.382 --> 00:03:41.778
To my astonishment both he and Conseil were soon asleep. I was wondering why they were so drowsy when I felt myself becoming very tired. My

42
00:03:41.779 --> 00:03:49.199
eyes closed despite my efforts to keep them open. I began to suspect that our food had been drugged. Evidently

43
00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:54.699
Captain Nemo felt that imprisonment wasn't enough to conceal his actions from us. I

44
00:03:54.700 --> 00:04:04.199
heard the hatches shut and thought I felt the Nautilus descending below the surface. I fell into a deep sleep filled with nightmares. The

45
00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:10.516
next morning I awoke with a clear head. To my great surprise, I was in my own room. My

46
00:04:10.517 --> 00:04:14.518
companions undoubtedly had been transferred to their cabin. I

47
00:04:14.519 --> 00:04:19.518
tried my door and it opened, so I was once again free to roam the submarine. I

48
00:04:19.519 --> 00:04:23.343
went up on the platform, where I met Ned and Conseil. Like

49
00:04:23.344 --> 00:04:27.589
me, they had been astonished at waking up in their own beds. The

50
00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:33.835
lieutenant came up and pronounced his usual phrase. There was no sign of Captain Nemo. Later

51
00:04:33.836 --> 00:04:38.748
that afternoon I was busy working in the gallery when the captain appeared. I

52
00:04:38.749 --> 00:04:46.502
hoped he might give me some explanation for the previous day's events, but he said nothing. He looked very sad. After

53
00:04:46.503 --> 00:04:50.645
a few minutes he said, "Professor, are you a doctor?" I

54
00:04:50.646 --> 00:04:57.883
was surprised at the question. "Yes, I am. I practiced medicine for several years before I joined the museum." "Then

55
00:04:57.884 --> 00:05:02.137
would you look at one of my men who is ill?" "Certainly,"

56
00:05:02.138 --> 00:05:08.391
I said, curious if this man's illness had anything to do with yesterday's mysterious happenings. Captain

57
00:05:08.392 --> 00:05:11.883
Nemo led me to a cabin near the crew's quarters. On

58
00:05:11.884 --> 00:05:17.915
the bed lay a man who was not only seriously ill but also gravely wounded. His

59
00:05:17.916 --> 00:05:23.978
head was covered with a bandage, and when I unwrapped it, I found a devastating injury. "What

60
00:05:23.979 --> 00:05:27.788
caused this wound?" I asked. "Does

61
00:05:27.789 --> 00:05:31.050
it really matter? How is he doing?" I

62
00:05:31.051 --> 00:05:37.447
hesitated to give my opinion, but Nemo reassured me that the man couldn't understand me if I spoke French. "He'll

63
00:05:37.448 --> 00:05:42.296
be dead in two hours," I said. "Nothing can be done to save him." I

64
00:05:42.297 --> 00:05:49.201
was surprised to see tears glistening in Captain Nemo's eyes. He said, "You may go now, Professor." For

65
00:05:49.202 --> 00:05:58.026
the rest of the day I felt upset. I slept badly that night and thought I heard distant music that sounded like a funeral hymn. The

66
00:05:58.027 --> 00:06:03.931
next morning Captain Nemo asked if my companions and I could go for another underwater walk. This time

67
00:06:03.932 --> 00:06:09.336
Ned decided to go with us because he regretted having missed our underwater hunt. Accompanied by

68
00:06:09.337 --> 00:06:14.352
Captain Nemo and about a dozen crew members, we left the Nautilus . I

69
00:06:14.353 --> 00:06:19.336
recognized at once that we were in the middle of a kingdom made of coral. Four

70
00:06:19.337 --> 00:06:23.011
of the men were carrying an oblong-shaped object. After

71
00:06:23.012 --> 00:06:31.320
walking for about two hours, we came to an area where there was a coral cross surrounded by small mounds of coral. Obviously

72
00:06:31.321 --> 00:06:34.582
the cross and mounds were man-made. And

73
00:06:34.583 --> 00:06:38.320
then it occurred to me that we were in the middle of a cemetery. The

74
00:06:38.321 --> 00:06:43.058
oblong object was the body of the man who had died the previous night. A

75
00:06:43.059 --> 00:06:51.645
grave was dug and the man was buried with great care and ceremony. Back onboard the Nautilus , I talked to Captain Nemo.

76
00:06:51.646 --> 00:06:54.637
"That was the man who died last night," I said.

77
00:06:54.638 --> 00:07:04.129
"Yes, now the coral will do its work and cover him for eternity." Nemo buried his face in his hands and tried to suppress a sob.

78
00:07:04.130 --> 00:07:08.121
"Your dead sleep out of the reach of sharks," I said quietly.

79
00:07:08.122 --> 00:07:14.321
"Yes, sir, of sharks and men," gravely replied the captain.

